{"ts": "2026-10-28T18:27:01.521324Z", "run_id": "r-20261028T1818Z-7356", "unit": "openspec:add-pdp-cedar", "seq": 34, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "add-pdp-cedar-fix-2/Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "The check's reason is a harness limitation (Python-only variation in a TypeScript project), so retry cannot help. I read the held patch itself (not citable, but readable in the worktree) and confirmed the two tests exercise createPdp -> loadPolicySet -> strictValidate with real assertions on code, stage, ids and message, matching spec scenario \"Each malformed policy is refused\" and design.md M8. The existing malformed.test.ts still carries the old M8 text, so the new file is the only test of the design's M8. The replay keeps all gates, so an accept risks nothing beyond the gate run. Whether a new test file is the right shape of fix for the finding is a verifier matter, not this harness question.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1"], "target": null, "kind": "harness", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.550149, "fix_unit": "add-pdp-cedar-fix-2", "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "cce1b0ed8f4b009bfd88815faa62f9c3d93bd6a9486007f26750fb849c3c7c0e", "checked": [{"ref": ".l4/config.yaml:22", "quote": "command: pnpm run test", "claim": "The project's test gate runs Node tests, so a check that varies only Python production files can never run for a change to a TypeScript test."}, {"ref": ".l4/config.yaml:48", "quote": "- \"**/*.test.*\"", "claim": "src/pdp/malformed.m8.test.ts is a test path under the configured globs, so the gate runs it on replay."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-pdp-cedar/design.md:116", "quote": "M8 `permit (principal, action == Action::\"reed\", resource);`", "claim": "The design's M8 text is the one the new tests load as the only policy of source m-src."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-pdp-cedar/specs/policy-engine/spec.md:22", "quote": "for M2 to M8, where M7 yields only warnings, `details.stage` is `validate` and `details.ids` is `[\"bad\"]`", "claim": "The scenario requires stage validate and ids [\"bad\"] for M8, which is exactly what the new tests assert."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/engine.ts:19", "quote": "const loaded = loadPolicySet({ schema: opts.schema, policies: opts.policies });", "claim": "createPdp, the function the tests call, runs the production loader, so the tests exercise real code rather than a fixture."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/load.ts:186", "quote": "fail(\"PDP_POLICY_INVALID\", \"validate\", ids.size > 0 ? [...ids].sort() : allIds);", "claim": "Only the strict validation stage produces stage validate with the policy id, so a loader that skips or zeroes validation fails the tests' assertions."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/load.ts:121", "quote": "fail(\"PDP_POLICY_INVALID\", \"parse\", [...new Set(failed)].sort());", "claim": "A parse failure reports stage parse with source ids, which the second test explicitly asserts against, so the tests distinguish the two stages."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/malformed.test.ts:56", "quote": "text: '@id(\"bad\") permit (principal, action == Action::\"read\", resource == Action::\"reed\");',", "claim": "The existing frozen test still uses the old M8 text, so the new file is the only test of the design's M8 and does not duplicate an existing one."}]}
